#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184009 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/id #uuid "2cb88713-f830-501e-9b0a-60320936ad14" :question/math-academy-id "e-4792" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\textrm A1] - [\\textrm A8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*If $\\mathbf{w}$ is a vector such that $\\mathbf{w}+\\mathbf{w} = \\mathbf{w}$, then $\\mathbf{w}=\\mathbf{0}.$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (w+w)+(-w) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{add [math]-\\mathbf{w}[/math] to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(w+(-w)) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the axioms of a vector space, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (w+w)+(-w) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{add [math]-\\mathbf{w}[/math] to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(w+(-w)) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom [math]{\\color{blue}\\text{A2}}[/math]}\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom [math]{\\color{blue}\\text{A3}}[/math]}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184038 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/id #uuid "132efc65-5f50-5582-8955-a5d34c57af04" :question/math-academy-id "e-8224" :question/problem "Let $V$ be the set of all real polynomials of degree exactly $3$, equipped with the usual addition and scalar multiplication operations. Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$V$ is **not** a vector space because $\\textrm{_________}\\,.$*\n\n- the sum of two polynomials of degree $3$ may not be a polynomial of degree $3$\n\n- $V$ does not contain the polynomial $-p(x)$ for every $p(x) \\in V$\n\n- addition of polynomials is not commutative" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer  is as follows:\n\n*$V$ is **not** a vector space because **the sum of two polynomials of degree $3$ may not be a polynomial of degree $3$.** *\n\nFor instance, if $p(x) = 1 +x^3$ and $q(x) = 1-x^3$, then $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ are in $V.$ However  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x)+q(x) & =(1+{x}^{3})+(1-{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =2\\notin V.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative.\n\n- For any polynomial $p(x)$ of degree $3$, the corresponding negative polynomial $-p(x)$ also has degree $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331332 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "042dc0fb-357e-59c1-8d04-096ccfbb7570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$F$ does not contain the zero element" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331334} {:answer/id #uuid "1ce21c01-f17a-54b1-beb0-cac4f6946d6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of functions in $F$ do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331335} {:answer/id #uuid "75f11239-8a13-52a6-b25f-87a13580da05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of $f,g\\in F$ is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331336} {:answer/id #uuid "824101ce-ad6e-5d33-8b0a-2323495b2b6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in F$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331337} {:answer/id #uuid "e1f13a8f-3c54-58b4-97f3-8683bc95d71e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of $f,g\\in F$ is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "042dc0fb-357e-59c1-8d04-096ccfbb7570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$F$ does not contain the zero element" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331334} :answer-field/id #uuid "1768b600-a256-5baa-8032-a21788f16c7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1cd61265-dcc6-5f89-bc03-f1168b91584b" :question/math-academy-id "q-106813" :question/problem "Let $F$ be the set of functions $f:R\\to R$ such that $f(0)=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$F$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$F$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **$F$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, evaluating the zero function $f(x)=0$ at $x=0,$ we have $f(0)=0\\ne \\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of $f,g\\in F$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of $f,g\\in F$ is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in F.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of functions satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331339 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4688d73b-9179-5ae6-ae97-603ba62dfce0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of polynomials is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331341} {:answer/id #uuid "b8eabd34-2b3b-55a1-96ab-ab60b97e5c23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331342} {:answer/id #uuid "e38ba574-7ad3-5ad2-81ce-e27fc819db61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of polynomials in $Y$ is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331343} {:answer/id #uuid "e13ec148-f3af-5f03-8b5f-2dbeeceac2c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of polynomials is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331344} {:answer/id #uuid "62aaa84f-a336-5fb0-96dc-f7020990aa8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1\\cdot p\\ne p$ for some $p\\in Y$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e38ba574-7ad3-5ad2-81ce-e27fc819db61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of polynomials in $Y$ is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331343} :answer-field/id #uuid "91cae22a-4346-52fb-a7f4-10f70ab881db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c206776-99db-55ba-ae48-7c0ec7d6d597" :question/math-academy-id "q-106929" :question/problem "Let $Y$ be the set of all polynomials in the variable $x\\in R$ with coefficients in $R$ of degree exactly $2.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$Y$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because **addition of polynomials in $Y$ is not closed.** *\n\nIndeed, let's consider, for example, the polynomials $p(x)={x}^{2}+x$ and $q(x)=-{x}^{2}.$ Then $p,q\\in Y,$ but \n\n$$\np(x)+q(x)={x}^{2}+x+(-{x}^{2})=x\\notin Y\n$$\n\n because $\\operatorname{deg}⁡(p+q)=1\\ne 2.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- $1\\cdot p=p$ for all $p\\in Y.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is associative. $\\,✓$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331346 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce898fe8-fd6b-5b52-9017-e65ffe00ec21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of functions is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331348} {:answer/id #uuid "b54006c2-3e06-5b4b-ad46-c76fc8f42806" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of functions is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331349} {:answer/id #uuid "89be815e-1f63-5f46-9e5e-f1df8575e80c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of functions do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331350} {:answer/id #uuid "4f5e12eb-b8cc-5911-a395-825117509f5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in I$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331351} {:answer/id #uuid "0b19a27a-a3ea-5832-a1a3-b2f087245cb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$I$ does not contain the zero element" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b19a27a-a3ea-5832-a1a3-b2f087245cb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$I$ does not contain the zero element" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331352} :answer-field/id #uuid "acf2c2d0-e9ec-5df9-897b-76e64f127228" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "17d56701-363e-5629-ba43-f0ff54124002" :question/math-academy-id "q-106933" :question/problem "Let $I$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ of the form $f(x)={2}^{ax},$ where $a\\in R.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$I$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$I$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication of a function by a real number) because **$I$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, $f(x)={2}^{ax}>0$ for all $x\\in R$ for any $a\\in R,$ hence the zero function $z(x)=0\\notin I.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in I.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws.\n$\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is commutative. $\\,✓$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331353 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46e9f705-09df-5d5a-9c36-b997e0546d99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331355} {:answer/id #uuid "2fd6f2fa-5ed5-5046-a077-b1c791ae5024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331356} {:answer/id #uuid "8bb61d29-1193-54bf-8920-cb61a6a85227" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331357} {:answer/id #uuid "599cddd4-d7db-5139-adaa-0ae2f9131ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331358} {:answer/id #uuid "2076147d-8933-53a2-bdb8-613d06226d4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fd6f2fa-5ed5-5046-a077-b1c791ae5024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331356} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cb8e73b-a644-5ef2-b66f-b49c5ba1f48f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dd84fbde-b275-5aa2-98b5-041f7a21abda" :question/math-academy-id "q-106938" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:*\n\n*Given any $x\\in V$, if $y$ is a vector such that $x+y=0$, then $y=-x.$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+y)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ y & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+y)+(-x) & =0+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =(-x)+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A1}\\,] \\\\ (y+x)+(-x) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+(x+(-x)) & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ y+0 & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ y & =-x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331360 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ebc974f0-9c54-57d3-8560-3d0e3e2cf25b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A6}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331362} {:answer/id #uuid "76007499-a2f9-5f38-a360-d7f526a899f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331363} {:answer/id #uuid "0c9b4075-08ac-5f90-92a8-0fe1d20845b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A7}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331364} {:answer/id #uuid "dbc3db7a-cc7c-5c43-8f37-ca233f6cf186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331365} {:answer/id #uuid "9da2369d-33f1-59bb-b54b-371eb1833f12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A6}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbc3db7a-cc7c-5c43-8f37-ca233f6cf186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331365} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e78fe80-7a3a-5054-b343-4552885d1013" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "258def85-3c26-5841-81d2-c1a1f3c916a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-106944" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*$0\\cdot 0=0$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =(0+1)\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A7}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{addition of integers}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A5}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A5}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =(0+1)\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A7}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{addition of integers}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A5}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184703 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2420a1a1-dd4c-5f7d-a312-35a9e5cf4e96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of polynomials is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183108} {:answer/id #uuid "51577410-6160-522c-9205-9abb45526d19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W$ does not contain the polynomial $-p(x)$ for every $p(x) ∈ W$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183109} {:answer/id #uuid "67cc8a1f-d027-5d95-bb4f-e91b729b3fe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W$ does not contain the zero element" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183110} {:answer/id #uuid "76898a5b-5be3-5841-8a7a-1f8e1195ab1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition of polynomials is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183111} {:answer/id #uuid "78561a3b-a374-507a-8dc2-675e93cda539" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183112}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67cc8a1f-d027-5d95-bb4f-e91b729b3fe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W$ does not contain the zero element" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183110} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a983190-e5b4-581c-80c6-c9780ac1d1ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183107}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ac2c9af3-5c5a-5bc3-898a-7e78bc1b3b9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-35558" :question/problem "Let $W$ be the set of all polynomials in the variable $x\\in R$ with coefficients in $R$ of degree $5$ or greater. Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$W$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$W$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to polynomials addition and multiplication of a polynomial by a real number) because **$W$ does not contain the zero element.** *\n\nIndeed, the zero polynomial has degree $0$, which is less than $5.$\n\nOn the other hand: \n\n- Addition of polynomials is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of polynomials is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- For any polynomial $p(x)$ of degree $5$ (or greater), the corresponding negative polynomial $-p(x)$ has the same degree. $\\,✓$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184704 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6544ed62-f78f-562f-9f00-66f3b6547b4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A7}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331368} {:answer/id #uuid "2c4cbfcd-8f5d-5fd1-b988-04afbf313569" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A8}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331369} {:answer/id #uuid "f87526fc-0602-5bbf-80ab-671ac26ae3bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A6}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331370} {:answer/id #uuid "b4629d94-f5d5-56ce-b7ac-559532877cca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A8}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331371} {:answer/id #uuid "b20569f9-1a21-5487-aa9d-f6ca9decc048" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A6}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4629d94-f5d5-56ce-b7ac-559532877cca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A8}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331371} :answer-field/id #uuid "93a3275f-a83e-5e48-9552-888ac595c23a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331367}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "45dd4a34-5d24-5e1b-9442-ff816cade184" :question/math-academy-id "q-35583" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*$\\alpha 0=0$ for any $\\alpha \\in R$*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0 & =\\alpha (0+0) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0+\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0) & =(\\alpha 0+\\alpha 0)+(-\\alpha 0) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-\\alpha 0\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0) & =\\alpha 0+(\\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =\\alpha 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0 & =\\alpha (0+0) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0 & =\\alpha 0+\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A8}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0) & =(\\alpha 0+\\alpha 0)+(-\\alpha 0) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-\\alpha 0\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ \\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0) & =\\alpha 0+(\\alpha 0+(-\\alpha 0)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =\\alpha 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =\\alpha 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85c6f6e5-4fb3-5bf2-9df5-d7a359e739e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A7}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331375} {:answer/id #uuid "55f4c348-8f34-53f9-bd7d-799cddd41196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331376} {:answer/id #uuid "4b61e1fd-47f4-539d-b2cb-37742b51f971" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A7}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331377} {:answer/id #uuid "090fbb82-f0dd-5293-8ff1-7e25fba362b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331378} {:answer/id #uuid "120f31c2-16f8-54b3-90a0-b99ea0569132" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55f4c348-8f34-53f9-bd7d-799cddd41196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A4}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331376} :answer-field/id #uuid "10a64892-d71e-5fea-9ec1-bf18a0f6b21b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0e20fac2-93b2-5854-b480-093fb40bcf26" :question/math-academy-id "q-35661" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement:* \n\n*If $w$ is a vector such that $w+w=w$, then $w=0$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (w+w)+(-w) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{add }(-w)\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(w+(-w)) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (w+w)+(-w) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{add }(-w)\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(w+(-w)) & =w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A2}\\,] \\\\ w+0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331380 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9bdb6bc9-47e2-5330-a1ee-270882f2aced" :knowledge-point/title "Proving Statements Using the Vector Space Axioms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86b35900-672e-543c-90f6-71d46bbf0ff7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331382} {:answer/id #uuid "627bf9ea-f8f3-5666-a6dd-a06e6dc7f01d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A8}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331383} {:answer/id #uuid "13a019dd-81c3-50c2-8bdf-843206c82272" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A5}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331384} {:answer/id #uuid "c1ae02d7-829d-5ebf-b37a-ec98c28f95b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331385} {:answer/id #uuid "e6091862-7070-50c8-a541-2b547644d399" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A3}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1ae02d7-829d-5ebf-b37a-ec98c28f95b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331385} :answer-field/id #uuid "315e32eb-cd35-53cd-a34d-73ef32dacbff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "629740cd-29bb-5969-bd61-3c1969786345" :question/math-academy-id "q-74671" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*If $x$ is a vector such that $-x+w=w$ for some $w\\in V$, then $x=0$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ x+(-x+w) & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{adding }x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (x+(-x))+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{adding }-w\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+(w+(-w)) &  & [\\,\\text{axioms  A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+w & =w &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ x+(-x+w) & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{adding }x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (x+(-x))+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0+w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ w & =x+w &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+w+(-w) &  & [\\,\\text{adding }-w\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ w+(-w) & =x+(w+(-w)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A2}\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A4}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0 & =x &  & [\\,\\text{axiom  A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186331387 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d9b62ae-7545-5d65-bcf7-74ab0e8662ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That Are Not Vector Spaces"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39860af3-1b79-5fdc-88d3-f97cfc645329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplication of $z\\in J$ by real  scalars is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331389} {:answer/id #uuid "33fd80c2-d4b2-5c36-9078-ae6103f2e2ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Addition and scalar multiplication in $J$ satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331390} {:answer/id #uuid "dfecf388-51e2-52e2-beb2-c0f9eef7ec6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$J$ does not contain the element $-z$ for every $z\\in J$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331391} {:answer/id #uuid "fd0d5d87-5022-5964-9962-bbe7d80e952d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition  in $J$ is commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331392} {:answer/id #uuid "23c65fa1-1ccd-53df-9697-e8bf7a6bbb51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "addition in $J$ is associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39860af3-1b79-5fdc-88d3-f97cfc645329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "multiplication of $z\\in J$ by real  scalars is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331389} :answer-field/id #uuid "be8584fa-8452-5218-be07-512f0778d847" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186331388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e96e196-0c41-5ca6-b712-3709509eeb35" :question/math-academy-id "q-94809" :question/problem "Let $J$ be the set of purely imaginary complex numbers, that is, complex numbers of the form  $ai,$ where  $a$ is a nonzero real number. Complete the following sentence: \n\n*$J$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to addition of complex numbers and scalar multiplication of a complex number by a real number) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$J$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to addition of complex numbers and scalar multiplication of a complex number by a real number) because **multiplication of $z\\in J$ by real scalars is not closed.** *\n\nFor example, if $\\alpha =0$ and $z=i,$ then $\\alpha \\cdot z=0\\cdot i=0\\notin J.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition in $J$ is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition  in $J$ is commutative.  $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication in $J$ satisfy the distributive laws. $\\,✓$\n\n- If  $z\\in J$ then $z=ai$ for some $a\\in R.$ Hence, $-z=(-a)i\\in J$   since $-a\\in R.$ $\\,✓$"}]}
